# THIS IS NOT A REFERENCE CARD. IT IS A PLACEHOLDER, AND IT IS DELIBERATE.
#
# `python -m mojolearn verify` compares the stage card this build produces
# against `kmeans.identical.fp32.v1.card` in this directory. That file does
# not exist yet, because nobody has run the fixture on a reference machine
# and installed the result. Until they do, `verify` exits 5 (NO REFERENCE)
# and says so.
#
# WHY A PLACEHOLDER AND NOT SIMPLY NOTHING. A missing file is a silence, and
# a silence gets read as "the packaging step dropped it". This file says
# which of the two it is, points at the procedure, and carries the token
# FILL-IN so that copying it into place under the real name still fails
# loudly (DEVIATION 925, see python/mojolearn/_verify.py). A shipped
# placeholder that silently passed would be the worst outcome this feature
# has available to it.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TO PRODUCE THE REAL CARD
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   1. On the reference machine, with a clean checkout at a known commit and
#      the IDENTICAL extensions built:
#
#        MOJOLEARN_NUMERIC_MODE=identical PYTHONPATH=python \
#          pixi run python3 -m mojolearn verify \
#          --emit-reference /tmp/kmeans.apple.card
#
#   2. Do the same on a SECOND vendor, at the SAME commit, and compare:
#
#        python3 tools/identity_trace_diff.py --labels APPLE,NVIDIA \
#          /tmp/kmeans.apple.card /tmp/kmeans.nvidia.card
#
#      If that does not print RESULT: IDENTICAL, there is no reference to
#      install and there is a finding to chase instead. A card from one
#      machine claims nothing across vendors, and installing one anyway is
#      how the whole feature becomes a number with no evidence behind it.
#
#   3. Install the agreed card as
#      python/mojolearn/reference_cards/kmeans.identical.fp32.v1.card,
#      delete this placeholder, and record BOTH runs in docs/VERIFY.md under
#      "Where the reference card came from".
#
# The full procedure, including what to do after a legitimate change moves
# the bits, is in docs/VERIFY.md.
#
# provenance: FILL-IN
# commit: FILL-IN
# device: FILL-IN
# peer-vendor-run: FILL-IN
